{
  "note": [
    "Real ADF, rendered HTML and attachment list recorded from a sandbox Jira Cloud site (2026-10-05) and sanitised:",
    "site, issue key, account, attachment, comment and media ids are placeholders; ADF localIds are dropped; dates are UTC.",
    "Shapes this fixture pins (they decide how a media node maps to an attachment):",
    " - an image or video pasted/uploaded in the editor is mediaSingle > media {type \"file\", id (Media Services uuid), alt = the file name};",
    " - the stored attachment is named exactly `alt` unless an attachment of that name already existed, then `<stem> (<media id>).<ext>`;",
    " - a non-image file inside running text is mediaInline {id, type \"file\"} with NO alt;",
    " - the rendered HTML links every file to its attachment: `<a href=\".../attachment/content/<attachment id>\" data-media-services-id=\"<media id>\">`",
    "   for a mediaInline, `<img src=\".../attachment/content/<id>\">` / `<object data=\".../attachment/content/<id>?stream=true\">` (no media id) for an image / video;",
    " - REST uploads keep duplicate names, and an attachment may be referenced by no ADF at all.",
    "The restricted comment is NOT recorded live (no project role of the sandbox accepts the test accounts, group visibility is off on the site):",
    "its `visibility` follows the Visibility schema of Atlassian's REST v3 OpenAPI document."
  ],
